"""ARCH-41 — Operational Seams, Automation Conformance & Extraction Memory.
One atomic, idempotent apply for all three tranches.

Run from backend/:

    python apply_arch41.py --check      # report every file, write nothing
    python apply_arch41.py              # apply
    python apply_arch41.py              # again: every line reads "already applied"
    python apply_arch41.py --rollback   # restore what the last apply replaced
    python apply_arch41.py --list       # the files this script owns

ARCH41-S1:apply. GENERATED from the real diff by gen_apply.py, which refuses to
emit if any file carries no ARCH41-S sentinel.

ACCEPTED STARTING POINTS
========================

  2f81cdf  "Production Hardening Phase"  (ARCH-41 not applied)
  6f7dc4c  "ARCH 41 TRANCHE 1"           (Tranche 1 applied)

Each operation names the sha256 of the ARCH-41 result and, for each accepted
starting point, either a list of ANCHORED EDITS or nothing (whole-file content
is carried). An edit's anchor must occur exactly once, and after all edits the
file must hash to the ARCH-41 result, or nothing is written. Large files
(llm_service.py, the verify chain) are therefore patched, not replaced, which
keeps this script reviewable and makes it refuse rather than overwrite a file
someone has changed.

A file already edited by a later milestone (ARCH-42 onward) is left alone.
Hashes are over normalised text (BOM stripped, CRLF -> LF); writes keep each
file's own newline style, BOM and permission bits. Everything is validated
before anything is written; a failure restores every file already written;
originals are kept under backend/.arch41_apply_backup/<timestamp>/.

Database: `alembic upgrade arch41_step1_extraction_memory` — run_arch41.ps1
does it, including the case where the held contract step already ran.

66 files: 30 carried whole (new), 36 patched by anchored edits, 0 replaced whole.
"""

